  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nAloft a cut off low slowly spins to our SE while shortwave ridging \npasses over the Great Lakes. At the sfc high pressure is centered \nover the northeast. Clear and calm conditions overnight and this \nmorning is leading to some fog development early this morning. Highs \ntoday will be in the mid-upper 80s rising to upper 80s to near 90 \ntomorrow. \n\nTomorrow and Thursday broad longwave troughing sets up over the \ncentral CONUS. Thursday a pocket of energy rounds the base of the \ntrof and moves a northern cold front closer to the area. Thursday \nevening and overnight has the best chance (40-60%) of convection \nprimarily over western portions of the area. Shear and instability \nquickly fall off after 00Z but any earlier storms could at \nleast be strong with 20-25 kts of shear and 1,000-1,500 J/kg of \nMLCAPE. Precip chances continue through Saturday afternoon with \nmore perturbations in the flow, though to a slightly lesser \nextent (20- 40%) and with less strong to severe capability.\n\nTemperatures stagnate in the upper 80s to pushing 90 through \nSaturday. Though things start to warm up again into early next week \ninto the lower 90s. The NBM probability of hitting at least 90 on \nMonday is >60% and the LREF probability of a heat index of at least \n100 is 40-60%. Tuesday the NBM probability of at least 90 is similar \nto Monday, while the LREF probability of a heat index of at least \n100 is slightly higher at 50-70%.",
